zark (1.0.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add zark(1) manpage. Source kept as Markdown in debian/zark.1.md;
    converted to roff at build time via pandoc + sed + awk in
    debian/rules. The pipeline normalises pandoc 3.x's bracket-form
    font selectors and drops redundant .PP after section macros so the
    output passes both `mandoc -Tlint` and `groff -ww -z` cleanly.
    Build-Depends adjusted accordingly.
  * Stop dpkg-source choking on tool caches in the working tree. Add
    debian/source/options with tar-ignore + extend-diff-ignore for
    .mypy_cache, .pytest_cache, .ruff_cache, .tox, __pycache__, *.pyc,
    .DS_Store and zark.log so a build never aborts with "unexpected
    upstream changes" after running mypy/pytest/ruff locally.
  * Stop bundling debian/ inside the .orig.tar.gz. The 3.0 (quilt)
    format expects a clean upstream slice; including debian/ produced
    a redundant overlay (lintian W: no-debian-changes) and broke the
    Debian-revision-bump workflow. The Makefile's `make dist` target
    now strips debian/ when assembling the upstream tarball.
  * Make lib/config.py the single source of truth for the version.
    The manpage source carries @VERSION@ in its header, substituted
    by both `make manpage` and debian/rules before pandoc runs (post-
    pandoc substitution would have to match the \[at] escape pandoc
    --ascii emits, which is fragile). The bug-report issue template
    placeholder and the example versions in debian/README.packaging.md
    were moved to a generic X.Y.Z form. Releasing now means editing
    lib/config.py and the two changelogs only.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Sun, 03 May 2026 12:00:00 +0200

zark (1.0.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian/Ubuntu packaging.
  * Distribution mechanism for zark on Ubuntu systems where the tool is
    used for day-to-day backups. The portable tarball workflow is
    preserved unchanged for live-USB disaster recovery — the .deb
    package targets the "install on the productive host" use case only.
  * Installs sources under /usr/share/zark/, exposes the entry point as
    /usr/bin/zark via symlink, and ships an example known_drives.json
    in /etc/zark/. The configuration directory search order in
    lib/config.py (env override -> portable etc/ -> /etc/zark/) makes
    this layout work without code changes.
  * Depends: zfsutils-linux, sanoid, cryptsetup-bin, gdisk, grub2-common
    and one of dracut | initramfs-tools — every external command zark
    invokes outside the recover-only path. Recommends pulls in the
    recover dependencies (dosfstools, grub-efi-amd64-signed, shim-signed)
    and the simulate dependencies (qemu-system-x86, ovmf).

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Fri, 01 May 2026 12:00:00 +0200
